# Advanced Inverter Features

## Grid Support Functions (Registers 181-250)

### Volt-Watt Control (Registers 181-184)
**Purpose**: Reduce PV power output based on grid voltage
**Implementation**:
- **V1** (181): Start voltage for power reduction (0.1V)
- **V2** (182): Full reduction voltage (0.1V)
- **Delay Time** (183): Response delay in ms/cycles
- **P2** (184): Power reduction percentage at V2

### Volt-Var Control (Registers 185-188)
**Purpose**: Adjust reactive power based on grid voltage
**Parameters**:
- **Vref** (185): Reference voltage for reactive power control
- **Filter Time** (186): Voltage filtering time in seconds
- **Q3/Q4** (187-188): Reactive power at voltage points 3 and 4

### QP Priority Control (Registers 189-192)
**Purpose**: Prioritize power quality over energy production
**Power Levels**:
- **P1-P4** (189-192): Power percentage at priority points
- Used for grid stability and power quality management

## Time-of-Use (TOU) Settings (Registers 202-210)
**Purpose**: Optimize energy usage based on time periods
**Configuration**:
- **Enable Flag** (202): TOU functionality on/off
- **Period 1** (203-206): Start/end times and charge/discharge rates
- **Period 2** (207-210): Second time period settings
**Use Cases**:
- Peak/off-peak rate optimization
- Grid demand response
- Battery optimization strategies

## Battery Management Advanced (Registers 211-216)
**Temperature Compensation**:
- **Coefficient** (211): Temperature compensation factor
- **Reference** (212): Reference temperature for compensation
**Equalization**:
- **Voltage** (213): Equalization charge voltage
- **Time** (214): Equalization duration
- **Interval** (215): Time between equalization cycles
- **SOC Threshold** (216): Minimum SOC for equalization

## Grid Stability Features
**Ride-Through Capability**:
- **Voltage Ride-Through** (217): Grid voltage fluctuation tolerance
- **Frequency Ride-Through** (218): Grid frequency variation tolerance
**Protection Systems**:
- **Anti-Islanding** (219-220): Grid loss detection and timeout
- **Grid Loss Detection** (221): Time to detect grid loss
- **Reconnection Delay** (222): Delay before reconnecting to grid

## Load Management (Registers 223-227)
**Load Shedding**:
- **Enable** (223): Load shedding functionality
- **Priority** (224): Load shedding priority levels
- **Voltage Threshold** (225): Voltage level for load shedding
- **SOC Threshold** (226): Battery level for load shedding
- **Power Threshold** (227): Power level for load shedding

## Implementation Guidelines

### Feature Configuration
- Read current settings before modifying
- Validate parameter ranges against hardware limits
- Implement gradual changes for critical parameters
- Log all configuration modifications

### Grid Support Coordination
- Coordinate Volt-Watt and Volt-Var functions
- Implement proper hysteresis for voltage-based controls
- Monitor grid conditions for optimal response
- Balance power quality with energy production

### Safety Considerations
- Implement failsafe values for critical parameters
- Monitor system response to configuration changes
- Provide manual override capabilities
- Alert operators to significant parameter changes

### Performance Optimization
- Use appropriate polling rates for different features
- Implement caching for frequently accessed parameters
- Monitor feature performance and efficiency
- Optimize response times for grid support functions
